00:00:03.129 --> 00:00:04.809 align:start position:0%
on the first of november two thousand  and six former russian spy alexander  litvinenko left his home in muswell hill  in london and traveled to the Millennium  Hotel in the center of the city there he  met two former KGB agents and Ray  Lugovoy and Dimitri Compton they had a  pot of tea waiting for him he drank only  a small amount during their 20-minute  meeting within hours he felt ill within  days he was in hospital he died in  intensive care 22 days later of  radiation poisoning a major operation  was launched and within days numerous  locations across London linked to the  former spy and the two men he met were  being investigated for possible  contamination that investigation was  widened even further when very small  traces of radiation were discovered in  two British Airways aircraft at Heathrow  Airport by the end of the inquiry  thousands of people had contacted an NHS  helpline dozens of buildings had been  tested and dozens of people tested  positive for contamination the  radioactive substance used was polonium  210 which can occur naturally but is  primarily produced in a nuclear reactor  only around 100 grams are produced each  year almost all of it in Russia
 

